---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import ProductCallout from '../components/ProductCallout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Buzzyfly"
	description="Why Buzzyfly exists and what the Digital System is actually for."
	pubDate={new Date('August 15 2026')}
	heroImage="/blog-placeholder-about.jpg"
>
	<p>
		Buzzyfly started from a familiar problem: too many tools, and nothing holding them
		together. I'd spend a slow morning setting up a clean process, feel good about it for
		about a week, and then watch it quietly fall apart the moment things got busy — a new
		client, a launch, a rough week. The tools were never really the problem. The lack of one
		place tying them together was.
	</p>

	<p>
		The Buzzyfly Digital System is what I built to fix that for myself first. It isn't
		another giant template pack you download once and never open again. It's a small,
		opinionated set of workflows for the parts of running a business that eat the most time
		and get the least credit — onboarding, weekly planning, and following up — built so they
		still hold up on the days you don't feel like running them.
	</p>

	<p>
		I try to run Buzzyfly the way I'd want a tool I paid for to be run: I use what I sell,
		I fix what breaks, and if part of the system doesn't hold up under real use, it gets
		rebuilt instead of just re-explained in nicer language.
	</p>

	<p>
		If you've already bought the Digital System, welcome — dig in, the framework is yours to
		start using today. And if you're just browsing, I'm glad you're here. I'd rather you
		look around and decide it's not for you than buy something that doesn't actually fit how
		you work.
	</p>

	<ProductCallout />

	<p>
		Questions, feedback, or something broken? Reach out — this is a small operation and
		real notes from real users are how it gets better.
	</p>
</Layout>
